                <pb facs="0531" n="411" sameAs="frus:frus1905/pg411"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Minister Dawson to the Secretary of State.</hi></head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Telegram.]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Santo Domingo</hi></placeName>, [<date
                            ana="#date_undated-inferred-from-document-content-and-sibling-dates"
                            calendar="gregorian" notAfter="1905-12-29T23:59:59-05:00"
                            notBefore="1905-12-20T00:00:00-04:40">undated</date>]. [<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Received December 29,
                    1905</hi>].</dateline></opener>
                <p>Gunboat <hi rendition="#italic">Independencia</hi> sent by Cabinet to Sanchez
                    with munitions has deserted and gone to Monte Christi. Will probably bring
                    expedition against Macoris or other point. Whereabouts of the President unknown.
                    The Vice-President arrives here to-day. French chargé d’affaires offers, if
                    agreeable to the American Government, to send Martinique for war ship to aid in
                    protecting lives foreigners which might be endangered by landing American
                    seamen.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Dawson.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
